  "body": "Found while testing #902 (not caused by it - reproduces without any unit change).\n\nOver MCP: build a job (import, stock, tool, one Face op, generate), `save_project` to a file, then `open_project` that same file in the same session. `get_job` afterwards lists **two** operations, and `post` writes the Face section twice - a program that cuts the job twice.\n\n`script::api::v_load` calls `project::load(&env.world, ..)` on the live world without starting a fresh document first, so the loaded entities land beside the ones already there (the GUI's Open presumably resets first). Reproduction: `crates/app/tests/mcp_units.rs::the_document_unit_is_the_posted_unit_through_undo_and_save` on the #902 branch, with a `get_job` operation count after its `open_project`.\n\nDone means: `open_project` replaces the document (as its description says: \"replacing the current document and clearing undo history\"); a test opens a saved project over a non-empty document and sees exactly the file's operations, and its post writes each section once.\n",
